## 3. Operating principles

- **Inspect first.** Before migrating any area, read the corresponding source files end-to-end. The decorator and middleware names above are a guide; the repo is authoritative.
- **Stage 0 before Stage 1, always.** Do not begin the Fastify swap for a route group until that group is decorator-free and green on Express. Do not interleave the two stages within one commit.
- **Preserve, then optimize.** First reach behavioral parity; only then apply idiomatic refactors. Don't do both in the same commit.
- **Phase by route group, within each stage.** Migrate one controller/resource at a time behind contract tests. Keep the suite green at every step.
- **Encapsulate.** In Stage 0 each former controller becomes a **plain Express router module** (function handlers). In Stage 1 that same module becomes a **Fastify plugin** (routes + schemas + route-scoped hooks). Design the Stage 0 module boundary so the Stage 1 conversion is mechanical.
- **One commit per concern, with the contract tests that prove parity.**

